{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVjskyF76HfwePWn4S68","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green CI + cached layer reuse tells you only that the *build command succeeded*, not that the addon actually rebuilt. The cache masked the rebuild step entirely.\n\nTo verify the addon was genuinely rebuilt against the new ABI:\n\n- **Force cache invalidation**: Add `--no-cache` to the Docker build or equivalent in your CI, run it once, and confirm the addon layer rebuilds. Then you know the baseline works.\n- **Check the build logs**: Look at the actual output from the native build step (node-gyp, cmake, etc.). A cache hit will show \"CACHED\" or similar; a real rebuild will show compilation commands and output files.\n- **Verify binary changes**: Compare the binary artifact before/after lockfile bump — hash it, run `nm` or `objdump` to inspect symbols, or check its timestamp. A true rebuild changes the binary; reused cache returns the same artifact.\n- **Add a CI assertion**: Include a step that captures build metadata (timestamps, hashes, or symbol counts) and fails if they match the prior run's artifact. Makes cache reuse obvious.\n\nThe safest approach for a lockfile bump: run CI without the cache once to confirm the addon actually rebuilds cleanly, then restore normal caching. That gives you the evidence you need before shipping."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6837,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6837},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"c0203328-b71b-437b-ad2d-408cf397d3ce","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:45:31.052Z","request_id":"req_011CdVjsjr2cVE4brK8DJNF5"}
